From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: no Dock, menu bar or hot corner from inside full screen

What: the other displays' full-screen windows ask macOS for the same
presentation as the main window (Dock and menu bar hidden, not auto-hidden),
and while the VM has the pointer in full screen the Mac's cursor never
reaches a corner of its display or the Dock's edge: within 200 points of
them it is detached from the mouse and QEMU moves it from the mouse's
motion, at least 3 points from such an outer edge (edges shared with
another display stay open). While detached, the guest gets the cursor's
new place, not the event's old one; the Dock's side is read again on each
full screen; quitting attaches the cursor again. Both follow the immersive option (on by
default; immersive=off keeps macOS's behaviour).

Why: in the user's 2.8.0/2.9.0 RC test the Dock came up at the edge of the
external display (its full-screen Space used macOS's default auto-hide), and
a hot corner set to "put display to sleep" fired from inside the full-screen
VM. The presentation option alone did not keep the Dock away on the other
display (tried), and moving the cursor back after it reached a corner did
not stop the hot corner (tried: the display went to sleep), so the cursor
must never get there. Local event suppression after a warp is set to 0
(else the cursor can stall after each warp). Known limit: a flick faster
than 200 points between two mouse events could still reach a corner;
detaching for the whole full screen would close that, but changes how the
pointer feels everywhere and was not tested with a real mouse. The
guest's pointer is absolute, so it only stops 3 points short of a corner.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's display windows; QEMU has one window).
Test: full screen on the MacBook and an external display: the pointer pushed
into each corner and along each edge shows no Dock, no menu bar, no hot
corner (notes: display-bugs track). Status: the Dock part passes. The hot
corner part is NOT shown: with posted motion-only events the cursor stays
3 points off, yet the bottom-left hot corner fired on every push in the
last test (also on a build that had passed 16 pushes before). A check with
a real mouse is open.

